  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`. After the front matter and the `# Habeas evidence` title, its first section is `## Workflow`. Nothing else comes between the title and that section. The section is an ordered list of eight numbered steps (\"1.\" through \"8.\"), written as checklist items. They run in sequence: stage files, check status, author, cover, check disagreements, report, commit, then move on to the next skill. The \"Testing and coverage findings\", \"Judgments\", \"Rules\", \"Fixing findings\", \"Disagreeing assessments\" and \"Gotchas\" sections all come after the workflow. The skill therefore opens with its workflow as ordered steps, before any other section. The requirement lists no violation queries, and I found no gap.",
